{
  "version": "0.6.1",
  "notes": "### Added\n- Notes show their area in the list and can be filtered by area. The note editor shows when a note takes its area from its project.\n- When some notes have no area, Settings > Sync and the setup assistant say how many stay on full devices only and let you choose areas for them.\n- Agents can set a note's area, create notes in an area and filter notes and calendar events by area.\n- Pyxida warns when the workspace folder is inside OneDrive, Dropbox, Google Drive, iCloud Drive or Box and offers a local folder instead. On Windows, the first-run folder avoids a Documents folder that OneDrive manages.\n\n### Fixed\n- If the workspace folder was deleted, Pyxida now offers to recreate it or choose another folder instead of showing an error on every view.\n- Recreating an emptied workspace folder or switching a device to full no longer treats the missing files as deleted, so other devices keep them.\n- Signing in to Sync again no longer uploads older copies over newer changes from your other devices.\n- A device with only some areas shows its real area names to agents.",
